This role is a permanent full-time position. As a specialist engineering electrical, you will be responsible for providing specialist advice and executes tasks associated with ensuring a robust change control and document management process exists and is followed in the Operation, to enable the accurate maintenance of the Operation’s blueprint, reflecting any approved modifications of its plant, equipment and infrastructure.
Other key responsibilities include, but aren’t limited to:
Develop technical documentation (incl. engineering standards, specifications, procedures, control system programs and drawings) from which the Operation is designed, constructed, operated, and maintained;
Governs and controls all technical documentation (incl. engineering standards, specifications, procedures, control system programs and drawings) from which the Operation is designed, constructed, operated, and maintained;
To provide a simple, integrated, effective system for change management;
To ensure that all changes or modifications to systems, plant, processes, projects, materials, products,
Provides specialist advice and executes tasks associated with ensuring a robust change control and document management process exists and is followed in the Operation;
To enable the accurate maintenance of the Operation’s blueprint, reflecting any approved modifications of its plant, equipment and infrastructure;
Analyses performance metrics and benchmarks performance across the function.
ABOUT YOU:
You will have experience and demonstrate capability in the following:
Must have a minimum of 3 years’ experience in an Open Cast Mining and Plant environment;
In depth knowledge of the Mine Health and Safety Act and Electrical Drawing;
Basic knowledge with level requirements, statutory legislation, and relevant internal and external standard
Qualifications for this role are:
NDip/BTech/Degree in Electrical Engineering.

RESPONSIBILITIES:
The incumbent will be responsible for:
Teaching undergraduate and postgraduate courses;
Mentoring and supervising postgraduate students;
Actively conducting independent and collaborative research and publishing research outputs in accredited journals;
Developing and/or expanding collaboration with academics internationally;
Initiating and delivering specialist courses at national and international levels;
Actively participating in administrative duties within the Department.
MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS:
Lecturer:
A Master’s degree in Statistics that includes a credit-bearing research dissertation and credit-bearing coursework consisting of core components that align with the required responsibilities of the incumbent;
An indication of an emerging research career with evidence of accredited publications in core components of the discipline contributing to the literature and scientific field of statistics; at least one recent publication in statistics in an accredited peer viewed journal;
Enrolled for a PhD degree in Statistics with proof of significant progress with the study;
Evidence of papers presented at national conferences;
Proven competency and experience are required in:
Teaching statistics modules and courses at both undergraduate postgraduate levels as a lecturer;
Advanced knowledge of at least one major statistical software programming language;
Implementation of efficient teaching models that would be applicable in the university setting.
Senior Lecturer (Same as for Lecturer, plus):
A Doctoral degree in Statistics
Proven record of curriculum development at the undergraduate and postgraduate level or other specialized professional courses;
Evidence of papers presented at national and international conferences;
Proven research publications in accredited journals, of which at least two in the mainstream statistical journals
Proven practice of advanced fundamental and applied statistical methodology.
Proven record of supervision of postgraduate statistical students
Evidence of supporting and participating in academic citizenship.
ADDED ADVANTAGES AND PREFERENCES:
In addition to the minimum requirements, the following will be an advantage.
Lecturer and Senior Lecturer:
Evidence of the relevance, impact and contribution of current research projects to the discipline of Mathematical Statistics/Statistics
Coordinating and teaching large classes of statistics service courses as well as core statistical modules.
Senior Lecturer:
An NRF rating.
